# Git workflow

- Never commit to `main`. Branch from up-to-date `main` as `wp5-surrogate`,
  `e02-loaders`, `fix-ads-logq` — roadmap id or bug, not `fix` / `temp` / `ai`.
- One concern per branch. Open the PR with `gh pr create` (base `main`, or the
  parent branch if stacked). Do not push commits to `main`.
- Commits are small and focused. The message says *why* (scientific or
  architectural reason), not "wip" or a file list.
- Before `git push`: `uv run ruff check .` and `uv run pytest` (or `make lint`
  / `make test`). A red `tests/test_exactness.py` is a stop, not a tolerance
  change.
- Results commits record git hash + full config + seed in the output directory
  (see experiment rule 10). Commit `uv.lock` in the same PR if dependencies
  changed — it is part of the reproducibility record.
- PR body: what changed, which roadmap item, how it was tested. Merge via
  `gh pr merge` only after the exactness suite is green.

```
# ❌ BAD — science on main, unverified
git checkout main && git commit -am "stuff" && git push

# ✅ GOOD
git checkout -b wp5-surrogate
# ... focused commits, make test, make lint ...
git push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create --base main --title "WP5: Ising surrogate" --body "..."
```
